758325577]'),(34,7,'A hash table works like a library\'s catalog system. Each book (value) has a unique call number (key). The librarian uses a system (hash function) to convert the title/author into a shelf location. Different books might get the same location (collision), so the library either uses overflow shelves (chaining) or finds nearby empty spots (open addressing). This system lets you find books quickly without checking every shelf.','[0.0177848469465971, -0.014296254143118858, -0.07774049788713455, -0.06342907249927521, -0.023099208250641823, -0.04617036506533623, -0.0005091085331514478, -0.02943156287074089, 0.1388488411903381, 0.007899625226855278, 0.024673691019415855, 0.12130019068717957, 0.09970765560865402, -0.0919305384159088, -0.10456008464097977, -0.028211267665028572, -0.029495790600776672, 0.011694696731865406, -0.04658193141222, -0.0677749291062355, 0.011739004403352736, 0.020254647359251976, 0.005653819069266319, -0.0067571415565907955, -0.048272136598825455, 0.030664751306176186, -0.02650090679526329, 0.005651363171637058, -0.038862500339746475, -0.09762238711118698, 0.02581649273633957, 0.07309132069349289, -0.02310967445373535, 0.03835776820778847, -0.11031730473041534, -0.011255637742578983, 0.005279017612338066, 0.05458397418260574, 0.04493885859847069, -0.07411828637123108, -0.07484039664268494, 0.020561452955007553, -0.05837124586105347, 0.054949238896369934, -0.06928350776433945, 0.07362311333417892, -0.05835900083184242, 0.021618489176034927, 0.020735548809170723, -0.026668308302760124, -0.03902621939778328, 0.03857070952653885, 0.016872458159923553, 0.034162238240242004, 0.04045913740992546, 0.05553511157631874, -0.05892644077539444, -0.05054405331611633, -0.02443605288863182, 0.015306910499930382, -0.029491012915968895, -0.02992384321987629, 0.04897541180253029, -0.01890553347766399, 0.0955907702445984, -0.011533425189554691, 0.037710756063461304, -0.001311248168349266, -0.00029473824542947114, -0.09786849468946456, 0.0759258046746